.SH NAME
lean-snapshot - Save a named snapshot of the current .env


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlean snapshot [name] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a named snapshot of the current .env so you can restore it later.

.PP
Examples:
  lean snapshot before-migration
  lean snapshot before-testing
  lean snapshot                  # lists snapshots (alias for lean snapshots)

.PP
Named snapshots live in .lean/backups/\&.env and can be restored with:
  lean restore before-migration


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for snapshot


